---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHero from "../../components/PageHero.astro";
---
<BaseLayout title="Your DMs deserve the same order system as your checkout." description="For online stores, Instagram sellers and WhatsApp businesses shipping physical products.">
<PageHero eyebrow="The Kora product plan" title="Your DMs deserve the same order system as your checkout." lede="For online stores, Instagram sellers and WhatsApp businesses shipping physical products." />
<section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-14 prose-kora">
<h2>The backend matters even without a shop</h2>
<p>Products, variants, reservations, payment records and fulfilment still need to agree. A stockroom can be your first inventory location.</p>
<h2>Start on Kora or connect later</h2>
<p>A Kora storefront is planned after the core workflow. Existing ecommerce integrations will follow selectively; they are not included in the first pilot.</p>
<h2>Make the handover visible</h2>
<p>Record packing, dispatch and returns explicitly. A paid order does not mean a courier has collected it.</p>
<p><a href="/pilot" class="btn btn-primary">Explore the founding pilot</a></p>
</section>
</BaseLayout>
